# Core Engine & Version Standards
- Engine Version: Unreal Engine 5.8.1
- Engine path (source build):
  `C:\Users\xondr\Documents\Engine\UE\UnrealEngine`
- Editor commandlet:
  `Engine\Binaries\Win64\UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe`
- Language: C++20 with UE conventions.
- IDE: JetBrains Rider with the Unreal plugin.

# General
- Never use `constexpr` for `FVector`, `FRotator`,
  `FQuat`, or other math types. `FVector` is
  `TVector<double>` and its constructors are not
  `constexpr`. Use `const`.

# Architecture
- `A` Actor, `U` Object, `F` struct, `E` enum.
- Use `TObjectPtr<T>` for UPROPERTY object pointers
  instead of `T*`.
- Use `UPROPERTY()`, `UFUNCTION()`,
  `GENERATED_BODY()`, and forward declarations in
  headers. Put includes in the `.cpp` when you can.
- A forward declaration is not a definition. The
  `.cpp` that reads a member or calls a method
  includes the header that defines that type.
- `TObjectPtr<T>` does not complete `T`.
  `AGameModeBase::GameState` is
  `TObjectPtr<AGameStateBase>`, and `World.h` /
  `GameModeBase.h` only forward-declare it. Include
  `GameFramework/GameStateBase.h` before
  `GameState->PlayerArray` or any other
  `AGameStateBase` member. Without it, MSVC reports
  C2027 and C2039.
- Server-only logic sits in `HasAuthority()` or in
  `AGameModeBase` / `AGameMode`.

# Startup state
- A value set once at the start of the game does
  not belong in `Tick`, `PlayerTick`, or
  `NativeTick`.
- Set it from `BeginPlay`, `ReceivedPlayer`, or
  possess. If that call runs again, return when
  the value is already set.

# Player input
- This project uses Enhanced Input. Keyboard events
  on a Level Blueprint do not receive keys.
- `APlayerController` reads keys in `TickActor`.
  Leave `PrimaryActorTick.bCanEverTick` true.
- `SetInputMode` during `BeginPlay` or
  `ReceivedPlayer` runs before the PIE viewport
  widget exists, so the focus is dropped. Apply it
  again after
  `UGameViewportClient::GetGameViewportWidget()`
  is valid, then call
  `FSlateApplication::ActivateGameViewport()`.
  Slate focus alone does not deliver `WM_KEYDOWN`.
- `UEnhancedPlayerInput::GetEnhancedActionMappings`
  is protected. Read mappings with
  `GetEnhancedActionMappingsView()`.
